-- The eliot repository as an Eliot package: the language's own layers, described in the format the
-- build tool reads. Inert so far — nothing resolves this yet (there are no version tags, and source
-- assembly is unwritten) — but it is where this repo's layout stops being folklore.
--
-- Every layer says `at`, because this repository cannot have the layout the convention assumes: it is
-- polyglot and always will be (the compiler is Scala), so Mill owns `lang/src` and the Eliot package
-- sits at `lang/eliot` beside it. The names stay `lang`, `stdlib`, `jvm` — what `//lang` selects is
-- the module, never its directory.
--
-- Not here yet: the `plugin` clauses naming the compiler-plugin jars each layer ships. They are exact
-- Maven coordinates plus hashes, and there is nothing published to name.

module lang {
  at lang/eliot
}

module stdlib {
  at stdlib/eliot
  dep //lang
}

module jvm {
  at jvm/eliot
  dep //stdlib
}

module examples {
  internal
  dep //jvm
}
